<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Alexander, Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Alexander was Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> from 1853 until his death in 1901. He continued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a>'s cultural tradition, supporting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-liszt">Franz Liszt</a>, founding an art school and restoring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> castle. His duchy joined the North German Confederation and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> during his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-alexander-grand-duke-of-saxe-weimar-eisenach.jpg" alt="Charles Alexander, Grand Duke of Saxe-Weimar-Eisenach" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotografie: Ludwig Held, Weimar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Held_Carl_Alexander_Sachsen-Weimar-Eisenach@Weimar_Schlossmuseum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
